    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup is anchored by two high-ceiling plays today: **Tyler Soderstrom** (76.91) and **Josh Naylor** (76.25). Both benefit significantly from facing a soft matchup against Imai and Pallante, respectively. **Tyler Soderstrom** is our primary offensive engine today, buoyed by a +10% park factor that elevates his power ceiling in a favorable environment, while **Josh Naylor** capitalizes on the same high-xERA pitching advantage to solidify his spot in the utility role. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (76.21) remains a near-lock at 1B, benefitting from a massive +19% boost due to Fedde\u2019s 5.36 xERA, ensuring our middle-of-the-order production is well-cushioned against quality-start risks.\n\nSpeed remains our priority in this 5x5 format, and while **Corbin Carroll** (60.21) faces a tough challenge against Gore, his ability to manufacture stolen bases keeps him in the starting nine despite a moderate platoon disadvantage. Conversely, we\u2019ve opted to bench **Trevor Story** (45.19) today; while he flirted with a starting berth, the combination of facing Wheeler\u2019s elite stuff and a low probability of successful base-stealing against a quick-to-the-plate catcher made him the odd man out in favor of higher-efficiency hitters like **James Wood** (70.66), whose leadoff spot and excellent xwOBA metrics make him a superior asset.\n\nWe are monitoring risk closely across the diamond, particularly with **Mickey Moniak** (54.09), whose score is suppressed by a brutal matchup against Skenes\u2014a starter with an elite 3.02 xERA and a fast release that severely limits our aggressive baserunning potential. **Gabriel Moreno** (47.45) also resides in a marginal tier as he continues to struggle with order placement and platoon splits. While we remain sidelined with **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Jose Caballero** on the IL, the depth provided by prospects like **Alex Freeland**, **Kyle Karros**, and **Carson Williams** provides a necessary safety net, though they remain on the periphery for this specific slate as we prioritize daily efficiency over long-term developmental upside.",
